# PREIshare — agent rules

## Project identity
PREIshare is a real-estate intelligence product: help investors make intelligent decisions. Prefer existing patterns in this single-package repo over greenfield frameworks. For mission, PR definition of done, and AI-use stance, read `docs/onboarding/team-orientation-notes.md`. For paths, read `docs/onboarding/repo-map.md`.

## Stack (do not substitute)
- Language: TypeScript (strict)
- App framework: TanStack Start + React (file-based TanStack Router; Vite + Tailwind CSS v4; npm)
- Backend/data: Supabase, PostgreSQL, pgvector (intended product data layer—do not invent config until it exists in-repo)
- Collaboration: Git + GitHub pull requests (feature branches; focused, self-contained PRs)

App surfaces today: `src/routes/`, `src/components/`, `src/styles.css`, `src/router.tsx`. Path aliases `#/*` and `@/*` → `src/*`.

## Where to work (new contributors)
- Safe first surfaces: `docs/onboarding/`, small clarifying `README.md` edits if mentored, other CONTRIBUTORS-style root docs the team already identified
- Read before edit: `docs/onboarding/repo-map.md`, `docs/onboarding/team-orientation-notes.md`, and any package/app README files that exist in-repo
- Avoid unless explicitly tasked: auth, billing, database migrations, CI secrets, large dependency upgrades, tooling (`vite.config.ts`, `tsconfig.json`, `tsr.config.json`, lockfile churn), and hand-edits to `src/routeTree.gen.ts`

## How to change code
- Prefer the smallest diff that completes the requested task
- Match existing naming, file layout, and TypeScript style in neighboring files
- Do not drive-by refactor unrelated modules
- Do not add new libraries unless the human explicitly asks and justifies them
- File routes: `createFileRoute` / `createRootRoute`; default-export components; prefer `Link` for in-app nav
- Style with Tailwind + CSS variables from `src/styles.css`; keep the scaffold layout unless change is justified
- Env boundaries: `createServerFn` / `createServerOnlyFn` / `createClientOnlyFn`; secrets via `process.env` on server only; client config only as `VITE_*` (never put secrets in `VITE_*`)
- Before Start/Router/Devtools edits: `npx @tanstack/intent@latest list` then `load` matching skills

## Secrets and safety
- Never commit `.env`, API keys, tokens, or connection strings
- Never print secrets into docs, rules, or chat logs
- Never paste private investor data or production credentials into an AI tool or pull request
- If a change needs configuration, document the variable *name* only (for example `SUPABASE_URL`), not a real value

## Agent workflow
- Restate the goal and list files you will touch before editing
- Implement in small steps; stop for verification after each logical unit
- When unsure about PREIshare structure, consult `docs/onboarding/` and the repo map rather than inventing paths
- Human remains the author: AI may draft; do not open work the author cannot explain

## Out of scope defaults
- No rewriting the entire app "for best practices" unprompted
- No changing product requirements silently—flag product questions to the human
- No parallel language, framework, database, or host next to the stack above
- No multi-feature rewrites or formatting-only churn mixed with behavior changes in one request
